{"name":"Tin Lizzie","hex":"#928a98","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tin Lizzie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of tin Lizzie.","A piece of waste ground near the railway, in Newcastle upon Tyne in the 1960s, where local children often played, and where Mary Bell killed Brian Howe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tin_Lizzie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ford Model T","blocks":[{"text":"The Ford Model T is an automobile that was produced by the Ford Motor Company from October 1, 1908, to May 26, 1927. It is generally regarded as the first mass-affordable automobile, which made car travel available to middle-class Americans. The relatively low price was partly the result of Ford's efficient fabrication, including assembly line production instead of individual handcrafting. The savings from mass production allowed the price to decline from $780 in 1910 to $290 in 1924. It was mainly designed by three engineers, Joseph A. Galamb, Eugene Farkas, and Childe Harold Wills. The Model T was colloquially known as the \"Tin Lizzie\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/1925_Ford_Model_T_touring.jpg/330px-1925_Ford_Model_T_touring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Model_T"},{"title":"Tin","blocks":[{"text":"Tin is a chemical element; it has the symbol Sn and atomic number 50. A metallic-gray metal, tin is soft enough to be cut with little force, and a bar of tin can be bent by hand with little effort. When bent, a bar of tin makes a sound, the so-called \"tin cry\", as a result of twinning in tin crystals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sn-Alpha-Beta.jpg/330px-Sn-Alpha-Beta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tin"},{"title":"Lizzie","blocks":[{"text":"Lizzie or Lizzy is a diminutive form of Elizabeth, sometimes given as an independent name in the United States, especially in the late 19th century."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lizzie"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg/500px-1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg/1280px-1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg/500px-1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1908 Ford Model T advertisement","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1908_Ford_Model_T.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Fordsidevalve.jpg/500px-Fordsidevalve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Fordsidevalve.jpg/1280px-Fordsidevalve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Fordsidevalve.jpg/500px-Fordsidevalve.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Model T engine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFordsidevalve.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/1920_Ford_Model_T_Controls_%281495288990%29.jpg/500px-1920_Ford_Model_T_Controls_%281495288990%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/1920_Ford_Model_T_Controls_%281495288990%29.jpg/500px-1920_Ford_Model_T_Controls_%281495288990%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View of the driver's controls, 1920 Mo